WEBVTT

00:00:04.589 --> 00:00:10.890
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the twenty-eighth. Usual quick run-through, once Teams decides we're all allowed to hear each other.</v>

00:00:12.199 --> 00:00:15.000
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, I'm here. Had the wrong headset selected.</v>

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:18.960
<v David Whitfield>You're coming through twice, mate.</v>

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:22.500
<v Olumide Adeyemi>There. Laptop speakers. Better?</v>

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:30.019
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, fine. More importantly, there's a birthday cake in the office. Quite a serious amount of icing.</v>

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.200
<v Jamie Brennan>That's breakfast sorted, then.</v>

00:00:35.509 --> 00:00:37.259
<v Sarah Okafor>Excellent nutritional advice from stores.</v>

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:42.840
<v David Whitfield>Would go nicely with a coffee, if the coffee machine in the canteen wasn't broken.</v>

00:00:44.159 --> 00:00:46.259
<v Priya Raman>Still? It's basically an ornament now.</v>

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:49.789
<v David Whitfield>Yeah. Just a moan, not offering to fix it.</v>

00:00:51.399 --> 00:00:57.700
<v David Whitfield>And the traffic on the ring road was ridiculous. Sat there staring at the same van for ages.</v>

00:00:59.979 --> 00:01:03.130
<v Fiona Doyle>I came round the other way. Not much better.</v>

00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:06.079
<v Aisha Begum>Proper Monday, then.</v>

00:01:06.829 --> 00:01:13.129
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before we disappear into the travel report, anything finished that we can get out of the way?</v>

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:20.280
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, already swapped the filter on the line 1 TCU yesterday. That's done, not another one for today.</v>

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:26.269
<v David Whitfield>Ah, that's the TCU one. I nearly mixed those two up.</v>

00:01:27.019 --> 00:01:29.120
<v Fiona Doyle>Exactly. line 1 TCU, finished yesterday.</v>

00:01:30.569 --> 00:01:36.519
<v Sarah Okafor>And separately, already swapped the filter on the line one HPU yesterday. That one's closed as well.</v>

00:01:37.019 --> 00:01:39.120
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Right, two different filters, both done.</v>

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:41.780
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep. Neither needs carrying forward.</v>

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:49.579
<v Jamie Brennan>Just an observation from nights: noticed the number two bearing was running a bit warm, but it settled down.</v>

00:01:51.299 --> 00:01:53.400
<v Aisha Begum>Settled back rather than staying warm?</v>

00:01:55.079 --> 00:01:58.930
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, settled back. Nothing I'm raising as a job off that.</v>

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:07.260
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Similar sort of thing from me. Heard a slight rattle from the Injection Moulding Line 2, nothing to action yet.</v>

00:02:08.759 --> 00:02:10.509
<v David Whitfield>Not a constant racket, then?</v>

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:12.830
<v Olumide Adeyemi>No, just slight. Observation only.</v>

00:02:13.699 --> 00:02:23.500
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. There is still a need to investigate the pressure drop on the water booster this morning. Low priority, to be clear. Anyone actually able to take that?</v>

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:28.949
<v David Whitfield>I can't get to the water booster until production gives us a window.</v>

00:02:30.849 --> 00:02:35.050
<v Aisha Begum>So access is the blocker, rather than us having someone lined up?</v>

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:40.400
<v David Whitfield>Yeah. I'm not taking it on with no access window.</v>

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:43.550
<v Fiona Doyle>There isn't a confirmed window to work against.</v>

00:02:44.319 --> 00:02:51.669
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Nobody taking the water booster, then. This morning is still the requested timing, low priority, but it's unowned and blocked.</v>

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:55.389
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Understood. Not quietly landed against someone's name.</v>

00:02:56.319 --> 00:03:02.270
<v Jamie Brennan>Um, I'll run a function test on the Compressed Air Dryer by the end of the week.</v>

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:10.659
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, Jamie. That's very much an 'if you've got a spare minute' one, not something to push other work out for.</v>

00:03:11.729 --> 00:03:16.979
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, spare-minute job. I'll fit the function test in by the end of the week.</v>

00:03:19.409 --> 00:03:24.310
<v Priya Raman>Just the function test, yeah? Not a strip-down dressed up as a quick look?</v>

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:29.819
<v Jamie Brennan>Just the function test on the Compressed Air Dryer. No mystery extras.</v>

00:03:30.409 --> 00:03:32.509
<v David Whitfield>Famous last words in this place.</v>

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:37.520
<v Sarah Okafor>No mystery extras in the agreement, anyway. Jamie's got that.</v>

00:03:38.849 --> 00:03:42.699
<v Fiona Doyle>I'll schedule downtime for the Cooling Tower with production next week.</v>

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:50.479
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Fi. Whenever you get a chance next week; no need to force it up the queue.</v>

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:56.699
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep, I'll do the scheduling with production next week, whenever I get a chance.</v>

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:03.250
<v Aisha Begum>That's agreeing the downtime, not saying we've already got a shutdown slot?</v>

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:09.150
<v Fiona Doyle>Exactly. No slot agreed yet. It's the scheduling I'm taking.</v>

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:13.009
<v Sarah Okafor>Good, Fi, that's clear.</v>

00:04:13.909 --> 00:04:18.110
<v Priya Raman>Right, I'll clear the jam and check the sensors on the Palletiser.</v>

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:24.439
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, talked over the end there. Sensors as well as clearing it?</v>

00:04:25.519 --> 00:04:29.720
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, both. I'll clear the jam and check the sensors. Normal priority.</v>

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:33.029
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Priya Raman taking the Palletiser, normal priority.</v>

00:04:35.399 --> 00:04:39.949
<v David Whitfield>Always tempting to call it fixed as soon as the stuck pallet moves.</v>

00:04:40.509 --> 00:04:44.709
<v Priya Raman>Mm, hence the sensor check being part of it, not an afterthought.</v>

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:49.310
<v Aisha Begum>And I'll send the shift handover report round by Wednesday.</v>

00:04:50.779 --> 00:04:54.279
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Aisha Begum. By Wednesday for the report going round.</v>

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:56.439
<v Aisha Begum>Yep, that's mine.</v>

00:04:57.199 --> 00:05:00.350
<v Fiona Doyle>Sorry, tiny bit of audio dropout. Was that Wednesday?</v>

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:04.240
<v Aisha Begum>By Wednesday, yeah. The shift handover report.</v>

00:05:05.459 --> 00:05:10.709
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. That's the lot. The finished filters stay finished, and the observations aren't new jobs.</v>

00:05:12.759 --> 00:05:15.560
<v David Whitfield>Nor the coffee machine. Especially the coffee machine.</v>

00:05:17.439 --> 00:05:20.240
<v Sarah Okafor>Your objection is on the record. Cheers, everyone.</v>
